What is NvMedia

NvMedia is NVIDIA’s middleware / API for hardware‐accelerated multimedia (image, video) processing on Tegra / DRIVE platforms. 
NVIDIA Docs

It provides surfaces (image/video), capture, encode, decode, format conversions, etc. 
NVIDIA Docs

It acts as a framework layer that calls lower‐level drivers for interaction with SoC components. 
NVIDIA Docs

Porting / Version Changes

NVIDIA publishes a NvMedia Porting Guide that documents API changes between DRIVE OS releases (e.g. 5.1 → 5.2). 
NVIDIA Docs

For example, in DRIVE OS 5.2.0.0:

The NvMedia IPP framework APIs are deprecated; moving to NvMedia SIPL APIs. 
NVIDIA Docs

Certain camera / plugin registration APIs are removed (e.g. registering multiple custom plugins per pipeline). 
NVIDIA Docs
